module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_running_unit_masked_loses_its_drop_ins_at_the_next_reload

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BelowCeiling, FoundBelowTheLadder, RecurringFailureMode, RungRead }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { StructurallyImpossible }
import gunbc.rung_climb { ClimbableButUnbuilt }

data a_running_unit_masked_loses_its_drop_ins_at_the_next_reload: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_running_unit_masked_loses_its_drop_ins_at_the_next_reload" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungRead { found_at: FoundBelowTheLadder, standing: BelowCeiling { current: FoundBelowTheLadder, ceiling: StructurallyImpossible, blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt, trigger_capability: "no built route constructs a mask of an active unit: every mask route reads the unit's systemd state and dispatches systemctl mask only on a proven-stopped unit. Sufficient for: no route the corpus builds reaches a running unit with a mask, so its drop-ins survive the next daemon-reload. The shared drain actuator's MaskWhileRunning admission arm is the sole remaining constructor that masks without that check, and it IS built by a production route: gunbc.runner.runner_host_file_converge's apply driver reaches runner_host_slot_actuations when actuation is admitted, and that leg (runner_host_drain_leg_decided over runner_host_drain_units -- every fabric member and required retiree) maps each DrainNow candidate to drain_and_mask_runner_slot_over, which supplies admission MaskWhileRunning, so a running fabric member or required retiree is masked while it runs. Retiring the arm alone therefore does NOT make mask-of-an-active-unit unconstructible; the follow-up node fleet-no-route-masks-a-running-unit, which routes that fabric/retiree drain leg through NeverMaskARunningUnit, must land with it." } },
  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a systemd unit that is still RUNNING is masked. `systemctl mask` reloads the manager, and a unit whose file is masked (-> /dev/null) loads none of its drop-ins, so at that reload, and at any later one, the live unit loses every property its drop-ins carried: the runner slot's memory caps (template drop-ins on srv1, per-slot system.control set-property drop-ins on srv4) and its Slice=. Its processes leave system-actions\\x2drunner.slice for a cgroup with no memory.max on its path.",
    "HARM: a required v2-bootstrap job on such a slot runs with no memory envelope; the envelope gate refuses it (MemoryEnvelopeAbsent at start, MemoryReceiptUnreadable when its unit's memory.events vanished mid-job), so the required check goes red on main and on every PR whose job lands there. Fail-closed, no wrong answer, but merges stall repo-wide.",
    "RECEIPT 2026-11-04, srv4, fleet-converge run 41861708547 (runner_host_file_converge at main 08d2cc56, gunbc#15819's slot-tree fold): the fold drained every out-of-date slot through drain_and_mask_runner_slot_over, which masks a busy unit and leaves it running (DrainWaitForJob). Twelve busy slots were masked at 16:22Z; witnesses runs 41861662327 and 41865951805 on main and 41866118627 on gunbc#15618 refused on srv4-01/02/08/12/15. Reported by quick-newt-573, loyal-deer-449 and silent-bee-845; loyal-deer-449 restored the units by unmask and restart.",
    "THE FALSE PREMISE IT RESTED ON, stated in gunbc.runner.runner_slot_actuation before this row: 'The mask comes first and is safe at any time: it only stops the unit being started again.' Masking is safe only on an inactive unit.",
    "REPAIR (slot-tree fold): gunbc.runner.runner_slot_actuation SlotDrainAdmission NeverMaskARunningUnit, used by gunbc.runner.runner_host_file_converge converge_runner_slot_tree: an idle unit is stopped BEFORE it is masked, and a busy or stopping unit gets no leg at all and stays pending, unmasked, for a later run. Witness: test.claim.runner.runner_slot_actuation_witness never_mask_a_running_unit_leaves_a_busy_slot_untouched_and_stops_an_idle_one_before_masking.",
    "REPAIR (cap bracket, node fleet-cap-bracket-keeps-running-units, 2026-11-15): the bracket's mask primitive gunbc.runner.runner_host_cap_bracket mask_slot_only_over no longer masks unconditionally. It reads the unit and dispatches systemctl mask only when the unit is proven stopped (slot_state_stopped: Inactive or Failed); a unit that is active, activating, reloading or deactivating is left unmasked (none). The bracket has NO stop leg, so unlike DrainSteps in the shared actuator it cannot stop-then-mask a unit whose job finished mid-wait; the only safe mask is on a proven-stopped unit, exactly runner_slot_actuation's NeverMaskARunningUnit. The old premise 'the mask inhibits successors and is safe at any time' was this class's invalid state held for the length of the wait. A running unit is left unmasked, and because the bracket has no stop leg nothing here stops it: its own restart policy returns it as a running idle listener, so the bracket ends in BracketAdmissionNotClosed, or BracketBoundExceeded once the wait bound is spent, and the cap write lands ONLY when every owned slot reads idle or stopped. On a host with a busy runner the cap write therefore never lands and no later pass changes that, which is a declared liveness cost of this repair rather than a temporary pending state. Draining a busy slot without masking a running unit is owned by the follow-up node fleet-no-route-masks-a-running-unit; its candidate mechanism is to suppress the restart for the drain (for example a runtime drop-in setting Restart=no) and then wait for the job to end, instead of masking. RED-on-main / GREEN-after control: test.claim.runner.runner_host_cap_bracket_witness a_cap_bracket_pass_never_masks_a_running_runner_unit -- a bracket pass over a fixture host with a systemd-active runner unit issues no mask for it, while a proven-stopped owned unit is still masked (so the control cannot pass vacuously).",
    "OPEN, SAME CLASS, NOT REPAIRED HERE: runner_slot_actuation's default slot_drain_plan (admission MaskWhileRunning) and drain_runner_slot_under_over (reached via drain_and_mask_runner_slot_over) still close admission on a running unit. A production route DOES construct them, contrary to what this row asserted: gunbc.runner.runner_host_file_converge's apply driver reaches runner_host_slot_actuations when actuation is admitted, and that leg (runner_host_drain_leg_decided over runner_host_drain_units -- every fabric member and required retiree) sends each DrainNow candidate to drain_and_mask_runner_slot_over, which supplies admission MaskWhileRunning, so a running fabric member or required retiree is masked while it runs. They remain the model's only remaining way to mask a live unit. The trigger is retiring the MaskWhileRunning admission arm; because that fabric/retiree drain leg is its sole production caller and is where the harm lands, retiring the arm alone would break the drain rather than close it -- the repair is the separate follow-up node fleet-no-route-masks-a-running-unit, which routes that leg through NeverMaskARunningUnit so a running fabric member or retiree stays unmasked and pending. Record only here. Nothing on these routes contains the harm (a masked-while-running unit's drop-ins are simply lost at the next daemon-reload), which is why the rung is read below the ladder rather than Mitigatable. These routes are outside node fleet-cap-bracket-keeps-running-units and are filed as the follow-up node fleet-no-route-masks-a-running-unit.",
  ],
  evidence: [],
}
